      "question": {
        ":question/id": "9c8020a2-1463-57fd-84c1-f1d6fcf52910",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\cos x}{10{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{\\prime}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\cos x$ and $v(x)=10{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(-\\sin x)(10{x}^{2})-(\\cos x)(20x)}{(10{x}^{2})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{-10{x}^{2}\\sin x-20xcosx}{100{x}^{4}}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\cancel{10x}(-xsinx-2\\cos x)}{\\cancel{10x}\\cdot 10{x}^{3}}\\\\ &=\\frac{-xsinx-2\\cos x}{10{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
